From: Anaconda recipe maintenance <pkg-team@anaconda.com>
Subject: [PATCH] keep -DCMAKE_JOB_POOLS pools when FLASH_ATTENTION_MAX_JOBS is set

The Ninja generator reads CMAKE_JOB_POOLS only while the JOB_POOLS global
property is unset. FLASH_ATTENTION_MAX_JOBS appends its pool to that
property, so every pool passed with -DCMAKE_JOB_POOLS disappeared from
the generated build.ninja and ninja failed on the targets assigned to
them. Seed the property with CMAKE_JOB_POOLS before appending.

win-arm64-only via meta.yaml patch selector (set from bld.bat).

diff --git a/aten/src/ATen/CMakeLists.txt b/aten/src/ATen/CMakeLists.txt
index 7f2f7fcb3d03..53ae71ce5dc5 100644
--- a/aten/src/ATen/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/aten/src/ATen/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -374,6 +374,14 @@ if(USE_CUDA AND (USE_FLASH_ATTENTION OR USE_MEM_EFF_ATTENTION))
   set_target_properties(flash_attention PROPERTIES POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE ON)
 
   if(FLASH_ATTENTION_MAX_JOBS)
+    # The Ninja generator reads CMAKE_JOB_POOLS only while the JOB_POOLS global
+    # property is unset, so appending here would drop the pools given with
+    # -DCMAKE_JOB_POOLS (ninja then fails on their unknown names). Seed the
+    # property with them first.
+    get_property(_flash_job_pools_set GLOBAL PROPERTY JOB_POOLS SET)
+    if(NOT _flash_job_pools_set AND CMAKE_JOB_POOLS)
+      set_property(GLOBAL PROPERTY JOB_POOLS ${CMAKE_JOB_POOLS})
+    endif()
     set_property(GLOBAL APPEND PROPERTY JOB_POOLS
       flash_attention_compile=${FLASH_ATTENTION_MAX_JOBS})
     set_property(TARGET flash_attention PROPERTY JOB_POOL_COMPILE
